theorem a-sum-of-defined-values-said-pointwise
  note        A sum's membership from a line saying its term at every
              index, whatever the term: nothing else says what a sequence
              by recursion's values are.
  let m ∈ ℕ                                                           (H1)
  let F(0) = 1,  F(k + 1) = F(k) + 1,  for k ∈ ℕ₀                     (D1)
         reads the counting sequence from 1
  assume for all j ∈ {1, …, m}, F(j) ∈ ℝ                              (H2)
  then Σ(j = 1 to m) F(j) ∈ ℝ

1.  Σ(j = 1 to m) F(j) ∈ ℝ
    membership, from H2
